  "body": " Which of the following correctly calls a function f with three inputs?    f = 2, 3, 4  This assigns the value 2 to f ; it is not a function call.    f(2; 3; 4)  Semicolons separate rows in a matrix, not function arguments.    f(2, 3, 4)  Correct. Function inputs are listed inside parentheses and separated by commas.    f = (2, 3, 4)  This is not valid MATLAB syntax.    "
